+Provider adapters own cost classification and source provenance; this change supplies no provider tariff or monetary value by itself. An SDK-backed adapter may accept a provider-owned mapper that inspects terminal SDK usage and emits the accounting chunk between token usage and finish. Safe-integer nanos bound one stored amount and every aggregate to `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`. Normal-Turn totals include failed and retried attempts when call snapshots cover each settlement or one final Turn snapshot replaces them. Session-title, compaction, and child-Session calls remain outside `modelCost`.
 
 Accounting extends Assistant settlements and embedded streams without changing model-visible history. Repeatable transient model statuses remain outside `AssistantStreamRecord` for predecessor compatibility and settle as a separately validated, timed top-level `statuses` timeline on `assistant/message` and `assistant/attempt`. The pinned predecessor can therefore open current settlements while omitting accounting and statuses; current-generation verification additionally enforces accounting order, top-level/embedded accounting equality, and exact status timelines.
 
